  "title": "How Can We Fight Blood Cancer More Effectively",
  "language": "en",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "heading": "Abstract",
      "text": "- Multiple myeloma is an incurable form of blood cancer. Over time, the cancer cells become resistant to the currently prescribed drugs.\n\n- Using the fully automated pharmacoscopy platform, ETH Zurich researchers are testing hundreds of drugs and combinations of drugs on bone marrow biopsies in a high-throughput process.\n\n- These tests show which treatment options combined with existing therapeutics would be possible for specific patients."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Reference",
      "text": "Kropivsek K, Kachel P, Goetze S et al.: Ex vivo drug response heterogeneity reveals personalized therapeutic strategies for patients with multiple myeloma. Nature Cancer 2023, 4: 734, doi: 10.1038/s43018-023-00544-9"
    }
  ],
